-HubSpot's default lead status options are New, Open, In Progress, Open Deal, Unqualified, Attempted to Contact, Connected and Bad Timing. An account can rename or add options, so the file must use values that exist on the account. The `docs/hubspot-probe.md` runs (the only real-service try; one free account, logs not shipped) showed one write (`OPEN`) accepted; the full list of default options and the write against our own portal are not verified.
+The three "Not written by the desk" rows rest on two facts in the repository: `src/lead_desk/crm_hubspot.py` calls only the contacts and contact-search paths of HubSpot (no lifecycle, lead pipeline or deal path), and the stage copy is tested in `tests/test_lead_crm_copy.py`, which asserts that the request body holds exactly the lead status and the owner id. HubSpot's own contact creation or automations on the account may still set other fields; that was not checked here. The list of default lead status options of a HubSpot account is an outside fact that this repository does not contain and that was not checked here; an account can rename or add options, so the file must use values that exist on the account. The `docs/hubspot-probe.md` runs (the only real-service try; one free account; from the author's own run, no log is shipped) showed one write (`OPEN`) accepted; the write against our own portal is not verified.
